.idea/
.vscode/
__pycache__/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
dca-engine/
*.png
!favicon.png
!apple-touch-icon.png
!social-preview.png
# Site imagery (landing mockups, proof charts). Everything *.png above is scratch;
# these are shipped assets and must be versioned or they 404 on Pages.
!assets/**/*.png
# Playwright visual-regression baselines must be versioned for diffing
!tests/**/*.png
*.bat
# ...but the scheduled Forward Log job is part of the site's upkeep, not a
# local scratch script, so it has to be versioned.
!refresh-forward-log.bat

# Local run logs. The _ prefix also keeps Jekyll from publishing them if an
# uncommitted copy is ever present in a deploy.
_logs/

# Local scratch scripts and their output. The _ prefix marks a throwaway probe
# (e.g. a post-deploy live health check) as opposed to a versioned build tool,
# so neither the script nor its report belongs in the repo.
/_*.cjs
/_*.txt

# Playwright / Node test tooling
node_modules/
test-results/
playwright-report/
blob-report/
playwright/.cache/
_commit_msg.txt

# Ad-hoc verification screenshots. The !tests/**/*.png rule above exists for the
# visual-regression baselines in tests/visual.spec.cjs-snapshots/; a _-prefixed
# capture is a one-off probe, not a baseline, so re-ignore it here (last rule wins).
tests/_*.png
scratch/reply-quant500-exposure-control.md

# Customer papers and the Art. 30 record of processing activities: pre-contract
# information, contract confirmation, RoPA, sales-log template and the PDFs built
# from them. Jekyll and the Caddy @private rule keep an underscore dir off the
# site, but a tracked file is still readable on GitHub - and the RoPA names the
# hosting and push-relay stack - so these stay only on the machine that sends them.
/_legal/
